# Vercel replaces .gitignore with this file, so the data lake has to be re-included by
# saying nothing about it here — the deployment carries gaia.duckdb inside the function.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist

# The COG rasters are 900 MB and nothing served reads them. They are pipeline inputs and
# outputs; the API answers entirely from DuckDB.
data/lake
data/manifests
data/claims.duckdb
# 448 MB of v0.1 pipeline scratch. Not read at serve time, and it was being uploaded on every
# deploy: the source upload was 567 MB, of which this was four fifths.
data/cache

# The v0.2 EII archive ships — the catalog and the component partitions are what every
# answer is read from. These four do not.
#
# The audit log is a write target, not a read one. The serverless filesystem is read-only, so
# a shipped copy could never be appended to; GAIA_EII_AUDIT_PATH points at /tmp instead and
# the log starts empty each cold start, which is the same bargain the claim ledger makes.
data/eii/audit.duckdb
data/eii/audit.duckdb.wal
# Validation inputs. The gate and the diagnostics read these; nothing served does.
data/eii/features.parquet
data/eii/terrain.parquet
data/eii/structure.parquet
data/eii/fuel.parquet
data/eii/labels
# Pipeline scratch: the fetched climate lattice, the spine, the rasterised index. 24 MB of
# things that exist so a rebuild can resume, and that no served answer reads.
data/eii/cache

pipeline/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.hypothesis
.git
